"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03236113739420639,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":47.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.012193293227210078,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":65.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.032763221263357935,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":45.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.0,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Empire State Realty OP, L.P. operates as a subsidiary of Empire State Realty Trust, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony E. Malkin | Chairman & CEO of Empire State Realty Trust Inc | Age 63","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 642 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers. Each employee generates $79K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $39K per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["Empire State Realty OP, L.P. Se is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.5B market cap on $768M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","The business throws off $51M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.62\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 700% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 30% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Among the least levered in Real Estate \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Empire State Realty OP (ESBA) Following A 17% Monthly Rebound Looks Cheap On Sales","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nysearca-esba/empire-state-realty-op/news/empire-state-realty-op-esba-following-a-17-monthly-rebound-l","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793871044.01,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier